[Music]  39 million visa-free travelers from more  than 60 countries are expected to visit  the EU in 2020  a new system should deal with these  travelers is called ETS the European  travel information and authorization  system non EU foreign citizens who want  to come to EU countries will need to  apply for travel authorization before  they arrive it will be an easy process  they have to go through and is just from  an online Trek which they can do it  prior to travel here's how a GIS is  expected to work travellers fill in an  online form and pay a 7 euro fee people  under 18 and over 70 won't have to pay  the application is automatically  processed it looks at personal data  travel documents and answers to  background questions like destinations  and contact information the application  is then checked against security  databases if the person poses a  migration or epidemic risks or a threat  to security access could be refused  Edge's authorization should be valid for  up to 3 years the most important thing  is to provide security and secure our  citizens this pre travel screening  should not cause hassle to travelers but  rather save their time and above all  lead to a safer Europe  [Music]

